<article class="profile" data-pagefind-body>
	<header class="profile__header">
		<p class="page__kicker">Meet the writer</p>
		<h1 class="profile__title">Scott Anderson</h1>
		<p class="profile__standfirst">Product engineer, co-founder and author. Building for the web since 2002, writing from the front lines of technology adoption.</p>
	</header>

	<figure class="profile__photo">
		<img src="/assets/img/scott-portrait.png" alt="Scott Anderson in glasses and a navy jumper, smiling at the camera" loading="eager" sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 26rem, 100vw" eleventy:widths="420,840">
	</figure>

	<div class="profile__body prose">
		<p>Scott is a product engineer and co-founder based in Melbourne, Australia, who has been building web software and SaaS products since 2002. As co-founder of <a href="https://floats.ai/">Floats.ai</a>, he builds AI-powered tools for recruiters, and through <a href="https://sirius.dev/">Sirius.dev</a> he helps candidates showcase their skills and find their next role. His career spans enterprise solutions for government and major organisations, CTO leadership, and founding multiple tech companies.</p>

		<p>With over two decades in the industry, from Java engineering at the Bureau of Meteorology to leading development teams delivering solutions for clients like the Australian Government Fair Work Commission and UNSW, Scott writes from the front lines of technology adoption.</p>

		<p>His book, <a href="{{ site.links.book }}"><cite>Future Proof: The White-Collar Worker's Guide to the AI Era</cite></a>, distils that hands-on experience into a practical guide for anyone navigating the AI revolution. This blog is where the thinking continues: shorter pieces on building software, running startups and staying useful at work as AI changes what work is.</p>

		<h2>Books</h2>
		<ul class="books">
			<li>
				<a href="{{ site.links.book }}"><cite>Future Proof: The White-Collar Worker's Guide to the AI Era</cite></a>
				<span>A practical guide for professionals navigating AI at work.</span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<cite>The Naked Truth About Working From Home</cite>
				<span>Available on Amazon.</span>
